        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Safety key, reset switch, outlet, cord,
            fuse — in that order, before anything else.</strong> Those five cover
            most dead treadmills, cost nothing to check, and take about five
            minutes. The console and the controller board are the last two
            candidates, not the first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Whatever the outcome, fit surge protection afterwards — the board is the
            expensive part and surges are how it dies. If the machine powers up but
            the belt does nothing, continue with
            <a href="/treadmill-turns-on-but-belt-wont-move/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">turns on but will not move</a>.
          </p>
